      "status": "full_text_read",
      "bounded_summary": "Sparse extrema-domain resampling offers low estimated compute and creative stretch behaviour, but the representation itself reduces spectral contrast and introduces nonlinear products. WSOLA won four of five listening items; transparent vocal or editing use is not established.",
      "verified_facts": {
        "corpus": "10 short TSM-toolbox clips; ratios 0.5, 1.2 and 1.8",
        "unity_mean": {"STOI": 0.91, "LAT_deviation": 0.09, "spectral_contrast_loss_dB": 3.08},
        "one_kHz_sine_THD_dB": {"odd": -38.1, "even": -85.8},
        "listening_test": "15 listeners, five items, no hidden reference; WSOLA highest on four items",
        "keyframe_scores": [51.1, 42.5, 48.8, 31.1, 46.8],
        "estimated_Cortex_M7_cycles_per_output": {"offline": 34, "live": 61}
      },
      "limits": [
        "Sparse reconstruction and time stretching are confounded without a unity sparse-passthrough control.",
        "Small non-conformant MUSHRA-style listening test and no dense full-rock mix.",
        "Poor singing-voice result and spectral-contrast loss on nuanced material.",
        "Long sparse regions can produce repeated material at silence-to-transient boundaries.",
        "Compute numbers are analytical estimates under stated assumptions, not a cross-platform benchmark."
      ],
      "citation_check": "partial",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "id": "S-ML-20260917-1500-04",
      "title": "Real-Time Neural Audio on Apple Silicon: Benchmarking Inference Frameworks Under Realistic DAW Contention",
      "authors": ["Dharanipathi Rathna Kumar Balasubramaniam", "Saravanabalagi Ramachandran", "Joseph Timoney"],
      "venue": "DAFx-26",
      "publication_date": "2026-09",
      "kind": "peer_reviewed_conference_paper",
      "url": "https://dafx.de/paper-archive/2026/papers/DAFx26_paper_16.pdf",
      "metadata_url": "https://dafx.de/paper-archive/details/rBxXewYH3YxRTiGXqSabwQ",
      "license": "CC BY 4.0",
      "read_depth": "full_pdf_all_8_pages_models_backends_isolated_and_contention_protocol_tail_results_state_and_async_limits_plus_current_repository_reproduction_docs_and_license",
      "status": "full_text_read",
      "bounded_summary": "On one M3 test system, isolated RTF failed to predict host callback deadline safety. Tail callback utilization, xruns and asynchronous inference underruns under realistic DAW contention are distinct deployment gates; backend ranking remains architecture, size, buffer and host dependent.",
      "verified_facts": {
        "hardware": "fanless Apple M3 MacBook Air, 24 GB, macOS Tahoe 26.4",
        "audio": "mono 48 kHz via BlackHole virtual driver",
        "isolated_configurations": 270,
        "TCN_L_128_RTNeural_XSIMD": {"isolated_RTF": 0.211, "host_p99_utilization_percent_zero_added_contention": 158.5, "xruns": 355},
        "TCN_L_128_BNNSGraph": "p99 below 20 percent and zero xruns across dimension A",
        "TCN_L_16_instances_anira_LibTorch_inference_underruns": 14022
      },
      "limits": [
        "One M3 machine, mono processing, virtual driver and partly flattened routing graph.",
        "Measured contention windows were about 15 seconds; temperature and memory were not recorded.",
        "ONNX TCN/WaveNet paths were effectively stateless and not behaviourally equivalent to stateful streaming versions.",
        "Random weights validate timing only, not sound quality.",
        "An anomalous RTNeural TCN contention distribution remains unexplained."
      ],
      "citation_check": "partial",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
